  m_TableData:
  - m_Id: 2300068806656
    m_Localized: TRAINING DOCUMENT
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 2300131721216
    m_Localized: REDACTION PROCEDURE
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 2300135915520
    m_Localized: Redact the name of the facility you were assigned to.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 2300135915521
    m_Localized: 'MEMORANDUM


      You will be sent to the [[Organization Training
      Center]].


      Click on a word to place a redaction bar over it.

      To
      redact several words in a row, hold down the left mouse button and drag across
      the text.


      Redact the name of the facility, then submit the document
      for review.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 2300135915525
    m_Localized: "Redact:\n\n\u2022 Names of Organization facilities\n\u2022 Hazard
      designations and types\n\u2022 Anomalous Fragments"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 2300135915522
    m_Localized: DOCUMENT No. 000
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 2300135915523
    m_Localized: 'JOB INSTRUCTIONS

'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 2300135915524
    m_Localized: 'Welcome to the {{Information Control Department}}, Agent.


      Your
      task will be to redact documents before they are processed by the {{Disinformation
      Center}}.


      Review the briefing and begin work on the document.


      Due
      to the growing number of {{"cognitive"}} hazards (including within the Organization''s
      own documentation), every document must be manually [[redacted]] by Organization
      personnel.


      When using your tools, such Anomalous Fragments will stand
      out from the rest of the text.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 192010200334336
    m_Localized: TEST DOCUMENT
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 192083919421440
    m_Localized: TEST DOCUMENT
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 192118518235136
    m_Localized: 'During an evening inspection, personnel discovered an [uv]unidentified[/]
      light trace in the northern section of the complex.


      Employee [magnifier]Smirnov[/]
      reported a brief image distortion on a surveillance camera.


      The access
      log contains the code [uv]SECTOR-ALPHA-7291[/], which does not match the current
      list of active passes.


      During a second inspection of Room No. 4, a
      [magnifier]microfragment[/] of unknown material was found on the inside of
      a ventilation grille.


      The word [redact,uv]CONFIDENTIAL[/] was also
      noted; it must be detectable with the UV lamp and must also be redacted.


      The
      designation [redact,magnifier]OBJECT-CASCADE-12[/], which reacts to the magnifier,
      was also found.


      For a combined test, use the entry [redact,uv,magnifier]EXPERIMENTAL-MODULE-OMEGA[/].'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 192144309010432
    m_Localized: "unidentified \u2014 long UV word;\nmicrofragment \u2014 long magnifier
      word;\nSECTOR-ALPHA-7291 \u2014 letters + hyphens + digits;\nEXPERIMENTAL-MODULE-OMEGA
      \u2014 long combined string."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 253372523921408
    m_Localized: DOCUMENT No. 000.1
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 253372599418880
    m_Localized: 'JOB INSTRUCTIONS

'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 253372599418881
    m_Localized: "Excellent work, Agent.\n\nAfter studying the {{cognitive}} hazard
      from your previous document, the Organization decided to use some hazards of
      this kind for its own benefit. The Research Department named them \u201Cmemetic
      agents,\u201D or \u201Cmemagents.\u201D In this document, you must leave the
      following [[memetic agent]], created from a {{cognitive}} hazard, unredacted:\n\u201C((THERE
      IS NOTHING NEW UNDER THIS SUN))\u201D\n\nFrom now on, [[read the assignments
      carefully]] for each individual document. Management will specify which memagents
      are intended for public release.\n\nStarting with the next document, you will
      begin your [[full duties]]."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 253372599418883
    m_Localized: "Redact:\n\n\u2022 Hazard types\n\u2022 Anomalous Fragments\n\nDo
      not redact:\n\n\u2022 The memagent specified in the document"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 266054698319872
    m_Localized: DOCUMENT No. 001
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 266054761234432
    m_Localized: Lake Creature
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 266054761234433
    m_Localized: 'On {{May 2}}, {{1933}}, in the ((Scottish Highlands)) region, the
      local newspaper {{Inverness Courier}} published a report about the {{Mackays}},
      a married couple who spotted a huge whale-like animal in the waters of {{Loch
      Ness}}.


      After the story began gaining attention, Organization agents
      were sent to the area. They were unable to establish contact with the couple,
      but other possible witnesses were questioned.


      According to the initial
      reports, the creature was about {{10}} meters long, had a neck covered in fur
      or hair that tapered toward the head, and a back with several humps. After
      conducting a reconnaissance operation, Organization agents discovered the bodies
      of {{5}} local residents on the lakeshore, dressed in robes. Their bodies formed
      a [[star-shaped symbol]], with a trail leading from them into the water.


      After
      discovering the bodies, the agents again attempted to contact the witnesses
      they had questioned, but the witnesses became extremely aggressive: they shouted
      incomprehensible phrases and attacked Organization agents. All witnesses were
      [[eliminated]].


      The Organization concluded that a cell of a [[currently
      unidentified cult]] exists in the region.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 266054761234434
    m_Localized: "Redact:\n\n\u2022 Numbers\n\u2022 Proper names\n\u2022 Anomalous
      Fragments\n\nDo not redact:\n\n\u2022 The region where the incident occurred\n\u2022
      Mentions of the Organization"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 266127087812608
    m_Localized: DOCUMENT No. 002
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 266127087812609
    m_Localized: BIG PEOPLE
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 266127087812610
    m_Localized: "In {{2002}}, a graphic artist posted a photomontage of the [[\u201Cexcavation
      of a giant skeleton\u201D]] on {{Worth1000}}. The image spread around the world
      as a sensation.\n\nThe Organization's AI agents began flagging the information
      as potentially dangerous and then attempted to contact the author. The author
      stated that he had previously worked for the {{Smithsonian Institution}}, which
      allegedly hides and destroys real skeletons of [[giant humans]] to avoid changing
      [[history textbooks]].\n\nOrganization agents arrived at the {{National Museum
      of Natural History}} in ((Washington)) to verify the information. They were
      met by the museum director, {{Rupert Lane}}, who gave highly <<contradictory>>
      information during questioning and denied the agents access to the museum archives.\n\nDuring
      the subsequent investigation, the agents learned that {{Rupert Lane}} did not
      appear in the museum's official employee records. When they returned to the
      museum, the subject could not be found, and a <<token>> bearing a [[five-pointed
      star]] was discovered in his office.\n\nThe Organization suspects a connection
      between him and the cult operating in ##Scotland##."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 266127087812611
    m_Localized: "Redact:\n\n\u2022 Numbers\n\u2022 Proper names\n\u2022 Anomalous
      Fragments\n\nDo not redact:\n\n\u2022 Geographical names\n\u2022 Mentions of
      the Organization"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 306465328381952
    m_Localized: DOCUMENT No. ...
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 306465340964864
    m_Localized: PERSONAL MESSAGE FROM MANAGEMENT
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 306465340964865
    m_Localized: 'T [[remendous work, Agent]]

      U [[nderstand that we appreciate
      the work you have done]]

      R [[est assured, you already understand how
      important your work is]]

      N [[ow Management is aware of your achievements
      and is promoting you]]

      B [decoder=WHY AREN''T YOU LOOKING AT ME?]UT
      THERE IS NOTHING NEW UNDER THIS SUN[/]

      A [[s a result, you are being
      transferred to a new facility]]

      C [[ommencing today]]

      K'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 306465340964866
    m_Localized: "\u2022 Follow orders\n\nRedact:\n\u2022 Anomalous Fragments"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1057939662618624
    m_Localized: DOCUMENT No. 003
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1057939662618625
    m_Localized: LINES IN THE SKY
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1057939662618626
    m_Localized: "Chemtrails (chemical trails) are a popular [redact,uv]conspiracy
      theory[/]. Supporters of the myth believe that the white trails left by aircraft
      in the sky are the result of [redact,magnifier]secret chemical spraying[/]
      intended to control the climate [redact,uv]or people[/].\n\nThis information
      was spread by agents of the {{Organization}} after stories about chemtrails
      became popular among the public and politicians. According to information obtained
      from classified sources, [redact,magnifier]none of the aircraft[/] leaving
      such trails appear in any aviation database. The tail numbers of aircraft leaving
      chemtrails [uv,magnifier]could not be identified either[/], as they contain
      [redact,uv]cognitive[/] hazards.\n\nOn {{October 2}}, {{2001}}, the {{United
      States}} Congress passed H.R. {{2977}}, in which the term \u201Cchemtrails\u201D
      is mentioned for the first time as part of a classification of exotic weapons
      systems. Congressman {{Anthony Watts}}, who proposed the term, is under surveillance
      by the {{Organization}}."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1057939662618627
    m_Localized: "Redact:\n\n\u2022 Numbers\n\u2022 Proper names\n\u2022 Anomalous
      Fragments\n\nDo not redact:\n\n\u2022 Hazards highlighted by multiple tools"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1057959837220864
    m_Localized: TRAINING DOCUMENT
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1057959837220865
    m_Localized: PERSONAL MESSAGE
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1057959841415168
    m_Localized: 'You are performing well, Agent.


      A new tool has been [redact]issued[/]
      to you: the decoder.


      To proceed, point the decoder at the following
      phrase:

      [decoder=issued]THERE IS NOTHING NEW UNDER THIS SUN[/]


      Then
      redact the word shown in the decoded message.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1057959841415169
    m_Localized: 'Use the decoder on the code phrase.

      Redact the word shown
      in the decoded message.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1057859786293248
    m_Localized: DOCUMENT No. 004
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1057859891150848
    m_Localized: STAIRS IN THE WOODS
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1057859891150849
    m_Localized: "In {{2015}}, a blogger using the name \u201C{{searchandrescuewoods}}\u201D
      on {{Geddit}} website described incidents from his work in a park-ranger search-and-rescue
      service, as well as stories told by his colleagues.\n\nIn one of his posts,
      he wrote: \u201CEvery time we were about {{50\u201360}} kilometers from the
      base, at some point we would find a staircase in the middle of the woods. It
      was as if someone had taken a staircase from an ordinary house, [redact,uv]cut
      it out of there[/], and [redact,magnifier]placed it[/] in the woods. The first
      time I saw one, I had a lot of [redact,uv]questions[/], but I was told it was
      perfectly normal. Now I just [redact,uv]ignore[/] the stairs when I come across
      them: it happens [redact,magnifier]very often[/].\u201D\n\nThe post attracted
      the Organization's attention. Agents were sent to national parks in the United
      States for further investigation. According to the information they obtained,
      these stairs act as \u201C[redact,magnifier]portals[/]\u201D to other [redact,uv]dimensions[/].
      In addition, [redact,decoder=Miles Marsh]one of the agents[/] stationed in
      ((Yosemite)) reported that his colleagues claimed that even without climbing
      such a staircase, simply getting close enough to it would bring trouble.\n\nDuring
      one rescue operation, an agent managed to locate one of these staircases, consisting
      of {{5}} flights. While examining it, he discovered a [redact,uv,magnifier,decoder=Cult
      of Five]star-shaped symbol[/] at its base and immediately reported it to the
      Organization. Further contact with the agent could not be established. The
      investigation is ongoing."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1057859891150850
    m_Localized: "Redact:\n\n\u2022 Numbers\n\u2022 Proper names\n\u2022 Anomalous
      Fragments\n\nDo not redact:\n\n\u2022 Geographical names\n\u2022 Mentions of
      the Organization"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  references:
    version: 2
    RefIds: []
